{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1460 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d09190c1c429751aabe24854df9a0e6a54e5416548e2351000e1c4526d6cf606" :edb/db-before-t 1459 :edb/db-after-t 1460 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534772 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:29:14.834Z" 13194139534772 true] [17592186068651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309117 13194139534772 true] [17592186068651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309124 13194139534772 true] [17592186068652 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309131 13194139534772 true] [17592186069097 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534772 true] [17592186069097 1100 "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{3x^{2}}{\\sqrt{x^{3} + 7}}dx$." 13194139534772 false] [17592186069097 1100 "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+7}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186069097 1145 "Let $u={x}^{3}+7.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+7}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+7}}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186069436 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534772 true] [17592186069436 1100 "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{3}-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186069436 1100 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{3x^{2} - 1}{x^{3} - x}dx$?" 13194139534772 false] [17592186069436 1145 "Let $u={x}^{3}-x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=(3{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{3}-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-x}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}-x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309118 13194139534772 true] [17592186309117 1089 "q-113711" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534772 true] [17592186309117 1100 "Calculate $\\int {x}^{6}(2+{x}^{7})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309117 1113 #uuid "434e8e50-5d62-5620-9685-e3a443ffb3fd" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309117 1145 "In this case, the term ${x}^{6}$ outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $2+{x}^{7}.$ But the derivative is $7{x}^{6},$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{x}^{7}.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =7{x}^{6}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{7}\\text{d}u={x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{6}(2+{x}^{7})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2+{x}^{7})^{2}\\cdot {x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}(2+{x}^{7})^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2+{x}^{7})^{3}}{21}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309119 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309120 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309121 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309122 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309123 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1041 "selection" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309119 13194139534772 true] [17592186309118 1110 #uuid "24affd62-b178-5ea5-8dec-3fc9a9a16cf8" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309119 1034 "\\frac{(2+{x}^{7})^{3}}{21}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309119 1111 #uuid "08d92a77-26d9-5f4b-8a06-af9599e0c6fc" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309120 1034 "\\frac{7(2+{x}^{7})^{3}}{3}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309120 1111 #uuid "0b5291b8-6c61-518c-af10-aee9d2c45ecf" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309121 1034 "\\frac{(2+{x}^{7})^{3}}{3}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309121 1111 #uuid "76dac32d-2727-5f1b-94cd-d1ac350a3564" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309122 1034 "\\frac{(2+{x}^{7})^{3}}{7}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309122 1111 #uuid "4bb08241-100c-51ee-a490-6f2fe0ae4c70" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309123 1034 "21(2+{x}^{7})^{3}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309123 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309123 1111 #uuid "0d364f12-b550-5d51-9f70-253dbfc50abe" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309124 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309125 13194139534772 true] [17592186309124 1089 "q-2379" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309124 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534772 true] [17592186309124 1100 "$\\int x{(3-{x}^{2})}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309124 1113 #uuid "deee0fb4-37d5-5821-a632-dfe38d0d54b0" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309124 1145 "In this case, the $x$ that's outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(3-{x}^{2}).$ But the derivative is $-2x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor. \n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=3-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\,⟹\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{(3-{x}^{2})}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {(3-{x}^{2})}^{5}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}{(3-{x}^{2})}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{(3-{x}^{2})}^{6}}{12}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309126 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309127 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309128 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309129 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309130 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1041 "selection" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309128 13194139534772 true] [17592186309125 1110 #uuid "60dd005e-b681-5f17-83eb-b24cbfd0713a" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309126 1034 "-\\frac{{(3-{x}^{2})}^{5}}{5}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309126 1111 #uuid "0fd3cb28-c1a8-5322-a4c6-b78331ea4a98" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309127 1034 "-\\frac{{(3-{x}^{2})}^{6}}{6}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309127 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309127 1111 #uuid "d8238967-73e1-54be-8880-188f9fc6c38d" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309128 1034 "-\\frac{{(3-{x}^{2})}^{6}}{12}+C" 13194139534772 true] [17592186309128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534772 true] [17592186309128 1111 #uuid "1c578af3-e34c-50b7-84ee-0e2b78fdda53" 13194139